  "title": "Family and People",
  "description": "Name the people in your life — the first thing anyone will ask you about.",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "u4l1",
      "title": "The immediate family",
      "goal": "Name parents, siblings and children.",
      "notes": [
        "mata and pita are formal/respectful. mammi and papa are what people actually say at home.",
        "Family questions are normal small talk in Punjabi culture, not intrusive."
      ],
      "items": [
        {"id": "u4l1-01", "pa": "ਪਰਿਵਾਰ", "roman": "parivar", "en": "family", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u4l1-02", "pa": "ਮਾਤਾ", "roman": "mata", "en": "mother (respectful)", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u4l1-03", "pa": "ਪਿਤਾ", "roman": "pita", "en": "father (respectful)", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u4l1-04", "pa": "ਮੰਮੀ", "roman": "mammi", "en": "mom", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u4l1-05", "pa": "ਪਾਪਾ", "roman": "papa", "en": "dad", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u4l1-06", "pa": "ਭਰਾ", "roman": "bhra", "en": "brother", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u4l1-07", "pa": "ਭੈਣ", "roman": "bhain", "en": "sister", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u4l1-08", "pa": "ਬੱਚਾ", "roman": "bachcha", "en": "child", "kind": "word"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "u4l2",
      "title": "Wider family",
      "goal": "Talk about spouses, children and grandparents.",
      "notes": [
        "Punjabi distinguishes the two sides of the family: dada / dadi are your father's parents, nana / nani your mother's.",
        "There is no single word for \"grandparent\" — you must pick a side."
